{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029901-sever-oaths-and-conditional-triggers","id":1029901,"title":"Sever Oaths and conditional triggers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T20:54:07-08:00","id":1029901,"title":"Sever Oaths and conditional triggers","content":"Sever Oaths (Fate 4, p. 139) allows the caster to change or dispel a conditional trigger. Since conditional triggers increase duration based on the probability of the trigger, if you change the trigger to one which more or less probable than the 'initial' trigger, does that change the duration of the spell?<br /> <br /> You can make Sever Oaths Lasting for +2 Reach, which would permanently change the trigger, but what if you don't make it Lasting <i>and</i> the new trigger still doesn't come around before Sever Oaths ends?<br /> <br /> My feeling is that changing the trigger should change the spell duration, partly because it feels right for taht to happen and partly to avoid silly shenanigans in which Fate Adepts cast with Conditional Duration using something like &quot;when the Sun rises&quot; for a large duration bump then change it to &quot;when Hell freezes over/when he willingly gives way his staff/(insert some other highly improbable condition here)&quot; with Sever Oaths in order to extend the duration of the spell without risking it being cancelled.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:33:20-08:00","id":1029924,"title":"","content":"I don't think it should change the duration, since that's set when creating the Imago and there's no precedent for modifying spell factors after the spell is cast (and that used to be an archmaster thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T00:37:37-08:00","id":1029952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029901-sever-oaths-and-conditional-triggers?p=1029924#post1029924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should change the duration, since that's set when creating the Imago and there's no precedent for modifying spell factors after the spell is cast (and that used to be an archmaster thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, that's true - but that does create a weird loophole around Conditional duration that allows a large bump with no real cost associated...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:03:20-08:00","id":1029956,"title":"","content":"As fascinating as the question is, &quot;conditional triggers&quot; are not the same thing as the Conditional Duration Attainment \u2014 Fabricate Fortune refers to the two things separately, and spells like Oaths Fulfilled or Sworn Oaths provide the most direct examples of the sort of triggers Sever Oaths is meant to mess with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:25:47-08:00","id":1030250,"title":"","content":"Aha! Thanks, that's a good point (and a much neater resolution).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}